  "problem": "In a cafe, there is a kettle and a microwave oven. The random variable $X$ represents the number of breakdowns per year of the kettle, and the random variable $Y$ is the number of breakdowns per year of the microwave oven. The probability distributions of $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nCalculate the expected number of breakdowns per year of both appliances.",
